Ghidra macOS ARM64 Native Decompiler
====================================

This product includes software developed at the National Security Agency
(Ghidra, https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The binaries in bin/ are compiled artifacts of the Ghidra 12.1.4 source tree
(tag: Ghidra_12.1.4_build).

Modifications made to produce these artifacts
---------------------------------------------

1. Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/Makefile
   The Darwin branch was changed so that the native helper binaries build for
   Apple Silicon instead of Intel:

     ARCH_TYPE:          -arch x86_64  ->  -arch arm64
     ADDITIONAL_FLAGS:   -mmacosx-version-min=10.6  ->  -mmacosx-version-min=11.0
     OSDIR:              mac_x86_64  ->  mac_arm_64

2. Build targets
   `make ghidra_opt` and `make sleigh_opt` were used. The upstream
   `make decompile` target was not used because it links against BFD, which is
   not available on macOS by default and is not required by Ghidra.

3. Installed names
   The build artifacts `ghidra_opt` and `sleigh_opt` are renamed to
   `decompile` and `sleigh` respectively, which are the names Ghidra loads
   from Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/os/<osdir>/.

No modifications were made to Ghidra's source logic, behavior, or network
access. No code from outside the Ghidra source tree was added.

